  "id": "COMPOUND:33837 - PROTEIN:60",
  "verbalization": "Calanphenanthrene A is shown to interact with multiple targets, including Serine/threonine-protein kinases B-raf and pim-3, which are implicated in the regulation of complement C5. These kinases are known to modulate the activity of complement proteins, suggesting that Calanphenanthrene A may influence the complement system through the activation or inhibition of these kinases. The evidence from the three paths indicates a consistent relationship between Calanphenanthrene A and Complement C5, with the target of the kinase being the key mediator of this interaction. The scores suggest a moderate level of confidence in this relationship, but further validation would be needed to confirm the direct involvement of these kinases in the regulation of complement C5. The mechanism appears to involve the modulation of kinase activity, which in turn affects the downstream pathways that regulate complement C5.",
